<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lydenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mashishing</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lydenburg is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mpumalanga">Mpumalanga</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, founded in 1849 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/voortrekkers">Voortrekkers</a> who left nearby <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohrigstad">Ohrigstad</a> because of malaria. It was the capital of the small Lydenburg Republic from 1856 until it joined the South African Republic in 1860. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> settlers negotiated land grants from the Swazi kings and were a factor in the politics of the region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lydenburg.jpg" alt="Lydenburg" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Slingsby · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dutch_Reformed_Church_Lydenburg.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
